{
  "$comment": "Golden vectors for catalog.proto DISPLAY RESTRICTIONS (Ross, 2026-09-26), from 0.4.0. Every image and its mask are shown to every viewer by default, in the owner's own views and in links the owner shares. A restriction (rule id, level image|product|source, subject, scope) only withholds; every restriction that applies to the image and whose scope covers the viewer context withholds what its scope names, so the most restrictive wins whatever the level, and each such rule is a denial the coordinator logs, even when another rule or a missing mask left it nothing to withhold. `image` lists the product ids that resolve to the image's head (the head first) and every source it was captured from; an image restriction's subject is image_id, a product restriction's any of product_ids, a source restriction's any of sources. `expect.image` and `expect.mask` say whether the caller is sent the image and its mask (mask is false when the image has none or is withheld); `expect.denials` lists the logged rules sorted by rule id, order not part of the contract. fc-coordinator's image-list chokepoint (GetProductImages, ProductCard.derivative_ids, any share projection) must agree with every case.",
  "contexts": [
    "owner",
    "share_link",
    "anonymous"
  ],
  "levels": [
    "image",
    "product",
    "source"
  ],
  "scopes": {
    "no_display": {
      "withholds": "image",
      "from": [
        "owner",
        "share_link",
        "anonymous"
      ]
    },
    "owner_views_only": {
      "withholds": "image",
      "from": [
        "share_link",
        "anonymous"
      ]
    },
    "no_share": {
      "withholds": "image",
      "from": [
        "share_link"
      ]
    },
    "no_mask": {
      "withholds": "mask",
      "from": [
        "owner",
        "share_link",
        "anonymous"
      ]
    }
  },
